---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.jsx';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.jsx';
import MachineCard from '../../components/MachineCard.jsx';
import FaqList from '../../components/FaqList.jsx';
import '../../index.css';
import '../../styles/machine.css';
import '../../styles/machine-m.css';
import '../../styles/business.css';
import '../../styles/inner.css';
import '../../styles/reading.css';

const title = 'Restaurant POS Software Price in India: What to Check Before Buying | Zipla POS';
const description = 'A practical guide to comparing restaurant POS software prices in India: plan terms, trial fit, billing, QR ordering, kitchen workflows, printing and support.';
const canonical = 'https://zipla.in/blog/restaurant-pos-software-price-india/';

const faqs = [
  { question: 'How much does Zipla POS cost in India?', answer: 'The Zipla POS Complete plan costs ₹4,999 per year or ₹11,999 for 3 years prepaid.' },
  { question: 'Can I test a restaurant POS before paying?', answer: 'Yes. Zipla POS offers a 14-day free trial with no credit card required. Test a small version of your own menu and service workflow.' },
  { question: 'What should I test besides the price?', answer: 'Test one real bill, payment marking, GST invoice output, relevant printing, QR ordering or kitchen handoff, and the owner review needed after service.' },
];

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    { '@type': 'WebPage', '@id': canonical, url: canonical, name: title, description, isPartOf: { '@id': 'https://zipla.in/#website' }, about: { '@id': 'https://zipla.in/#software' }, inLanguage: 'en-IN', dateModified: '2026-09-22', breadcrumb: { '@id': `${canonical}#breadcrumb` } },
    { '@type': 'BreadcrumbList', '@id': `${canonical}#breadcrumb`, itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://zipla.in/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Blog', item: 'https://zipla.in/blog/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Restaurant POS Software Price in India', item: canonical },
    ] },
    { '@type': 'Article', '@id': `${canonical}#article`, headline: title, description, url: canonical, datePublished: '2026-09-22', dateModified: '2026-09-22', author: { '@id': 'https://zipla.in/#organization' }, publisher: { '@id': 'https://zipla.in/#organization' }, inLanguage: 'en-IN' },
    { '@type': 'FAQPage', '@id': `${canonical}#faq`, mainEntity: faqs.map((faq) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: faq.question, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: faq.answer } })) },
  ],
};
---

<Layout zp title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <Header client:load />
  <main class="zb-page">
    <nav class="zb-wrap zb-crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">›</span><a href="/blog/">Blog</a><span aria-hidden="true">›</span><span>Restaurant POS Pricing</span></nav>

    <article>
      <header class="zb-wrap zm-hero-m zr-hero">
        <div class="zm-hero-top">
          <p class="zr-meta"><span class="zr-tag">Buying guide</span></p>
          <h1 class="zb-h1">Restaurant POS Software Price in India: <span class="zb-hl">What to Check Before Buying</span></h1>
        <p class="zb-lede"><strong>Short answer:</strong> Compare restaurant POS software on the workflow it supports, not only the displayed price. Check billing, GST invoice output, payment marking, relevant kitchen or QR features, printing, trial terms and support before you commit.</p>
        <p class="zi-dateline"><strong>Last reviewed:</strong> <time datetime="2026-09-22">22 September 2026</time> · For Indian restaurant, café, QSR, bakery, sweet-shop and dhaba owners.</p>
        </div>
        <MachineCard />
      </header>

      <div class="zb-wrap zr-body">
        <div class="zr-read">
        <p>Restaurant POS pricing in India can look simple until you compare what a plan actually lets your team do during a busy service. A low annual price is not useful if the workflow does not fit your menu, payment modes, printer or kitchen handoff.</p>
        <p>This guide gives a practical way to compare a restaurant POS before buying. It uses current Zipla POS plan facts where stated and avoids treating a feature list as proof of a business result.</p>

        <h2>What should a restaurant POS price include?</h2>
        <p>Start by writing down the steps your team performs every day. A useful comparison should make these questions easy to answer:</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Can the counter team create a bill from the real menu?</li>
          <li>Can the business configure GST invoices and mark cash, UPI or card payments?</li>
          <li>Does the outlet need table QR ordering, Customer QR Home Ordering or a kitchen queue?</li>
          <li>Can the team print on a compatible Bluetooth thermal printer or share a bill on WhatsApp?</li>
          <li>What can the owner review after service, such as sales and payment-mode information?</li>
          <li>Is there a trial long enough to test the outlet’s own menu?</li>
        </ol>

        <h2>What is Zipla POS pricing?</h2>
        <p>Zipla POS has one current Complete plan for the listed restaurant workflows:</p>
        <div class="zr-fact"><strong>₹4,999 per year</strong><span>or ₹11,999 for 3 years prepaid</span><span>14-day free trial · No credit card required</span></div>
        <p>The Complete plan covers counter billing, configured GST invoices, payment tracking, inventory with low-stock alerts, staff roles, table QR ordering, Customer QR Home Ordering, KDS, Bluetooth KOT auto-print, sales analytics and day-close reports. See the full <a href="/pricing/">Zipla POS pricing page</a> for the current terms.</p>

        <h2>Seven checks to make before choosing</h2>
        <h3>1. Test the real menu</h3><p>Add a small set of genuine items, prices and categories. A sample screen cannot tell you whether your actual menu is easy for staff to use.</p>
        <h3>2. Test one complete bill</h3><p>Create one customer bill, mark the payment mode and review the invoice output. Include the tax and business details your outlet actually uses.</p>
        <h3>3. Check the kitchen handoff</h3><p>If your team uses a kitchen queue, test KDS and Bluetooth KOT auto-print during the same workflow. If it is a counter-only outlet, do not pay for a workflow you will not use.</p>
        <h3>4. Check QR ordering fit</h3><p>Table QR ordering and Customer QR Home Ordering are different use cases. Decide whether the order starts at a table or from a customer’s home before comparing plans.</p>
        <h3>5. Check printer compatibility</h3><p>Confirm the printer connection and paper size you intend to use. Zipla POS supports compatible 58mm and 80mm Bluetooth thermal printers.</p>
        <h3>6. Understand connectivity limits</h3><p>After the menu has loaded, bills can be created without an active internet connection. UPI and other online payments require connectivity.</p>
        <h3>7. Check owner review</h3><p>After the shift, review the sales analytics and day-close information that the owner or manager needs. This is part of the buying decision, not an afterthought.</p>
        <h2>Is a cheaper POS always the better choice?</h2>
        <p>No. The right comparison is the total fit for the outlet: plan price, included workflow, setup effort, printing, support and the time required for staff to use it correctly. A transparent trial is more useful than choosing from a price table alone.</p>
        <p>For a product-specific comparison, read the <a href="/restaurant-pos-software/">restaurant POS software guide</a> and the <a href="/faq/">Zipla POS FAQ</a>. For GST questions, use the separate <a href="/blog/restaurant-dhaba-gst-invoice-guide-2026/">restaurant and dhaba GST invoice guide</a>.</p>

        <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <FaqList faqs={faqs} heading="h3" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="ink zb-ink">
        <div class="zb-wrap zb-sec zb-demo">
          <div class="zb-demo-l"><h2 class="zb-demo-h">Test the plan with your own menu</h2><p class="zb-demo-p">Start a 14-day free trial without a credit card, or discuss your counter, QR and kitchen workflow on WhatsApp.</p></div>
          <div class="zb-demo-r"><a class="zb-btn zb-btn-gold zb-btn-lg zb-btn-wide" href="https://app.zipla.in/register">Start Free Trial</a><a class="zb-btn zb-btn-ghost zb-btn-lg zb-btn-wide" href="/pricing/">See Pricing</a></div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
